              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do endurance athletes need protein powder?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not always, but it is useful. Endurance athletes typically need about 1.2 to 1.6 g of protein per kilogram daily, more in heavy blocks, mainly for repair and adaptation. After long sessions, combining protein with carbohydrate supports recovery and glycogen restoration. A certified whey isolate mixed with fruit or a carbohydrate drink is a convenient way to do it.
